public import Theory.SpecificGroups.ClassicalOrthogonal.SplitOdd.BinaryEightObstruction.Simplicity.Geometry.Coordinates

/-!
# Certified singular-vector and stabilizer orbits in binary split eight-space

Short traces of actual Siegel roots transport `e₀` to every nonzero singular
vector, `e₁` to every other singular vector perpendicular to `e₀`, and `f₀` to
every singular vector not perpendicular to `e₀`. The last two trace families
fix `e₀`. The three exported transport theorems are unconditional statements
about the actual natural linear action.

Each intermediate root step is checked in Lean's kernel. The encoder theorem
in `Coordinates` and the universal byte checks below prove coverage. Neither
Python nor an assumed group order supplies a mathematical premise.

Generated by `Geometry/source/generate.py`; mathematical consumers are in
`Simplicity/Geometry.lean`.
-/

